nificantly more effective than placebo in IIEF-overall satisfaction, SEP2 and SEP3 scores", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:09:38.04Z'), source_document:"SECTION 8: SPECIAL POPULATIONS", source:"section-3-treatment.md"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:22}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"→ PDE5i (phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors)", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:07:48.806Z'), source_document:"SECTION 1: CLINICAL DECISION ALGORITHMS", source:"section-1-algorithm.md"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:91}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"If initial treatments (e.g. lifestyle changes, oral medications like PDE5i, or other conservative measures) do not yield satisfactory results,", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:11:00.607Z'), source_document:"SECTION 7: REFERRAL", source:"section-7-referral.md"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:157}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"PDE5i was more effective than placebo post-nerve sparing open radical prostatectomy (OR=10.09)", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:11:19.313Z'), source_document:"SECTION 8: SPECIAL POPULATIONS", source:"section-8-special-populations.md"}}, {start: {_id:21}, end: {_id:162}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"PDE5i: Improved erection, sexual intercourse frequency, satisfaction, enjoyment, desire, overall sex life, sexual relationship and self-confidence", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:11:19.466Z'), source_document:"SECTION 8: SPECIAL POPULATIONS", source:"section-8-special-populations.md"}}, {start: {_id:84}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"The main pharmacological agents for ED are phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors (PDE5is).", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:09:37.849Z'), source_document:"SECTION 4: TREATMENT", source:"section-3-treatment.md"}}, {start: {_id:88}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Intracavernosal Injection (ICI) | First medical treatment for ED; only FDA-approved preparation is alprostadil", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:09:38.325Z'), source_document:"SECTION 4: TREATMENT", source:"section-3-treatment.md"}}, {start: {_id:89}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Intraurethral Alprostadil | Two methods of administration", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:09:38.397Z'), source_document:"SECTION 3: TREATMENT", source:"section-3-treatment.md"}}, {start: {_id:109}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Combination of PDE5i with various agents (alpha-blocker, testosterone, antioxidants) was more effective than PDE5i monotherapy", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:10:15.581Z'), source_document:"SECTION 4: TREATMENT", source:"section-4-treatment.md"}}, {start: {_id:110}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Combination therapy of PDE5i and antioxidants (e.g. propionyl-L-carnitine or L-arginine) with PDE5i monotherapy in patients mainly with ED showed: Combination therapy was more effective based on IIEF score", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:10:32.322Z'), source_document:"SECTION 5: TRADITIONAL AND COMPLEMENTARY MEDICINE", source:"section-5-tcm.md"}}, {start: {_id:111}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"A meta-analysis of seven RCTs demonstrated the effectiveness of red ginseng in the treatment of ED compared with placebo", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:10:32.345Z'), source_document:"SECTION 5: TRADITIONAL AND COMPLEMENTARY MEDICINE", source:"section-5-tcm.md"}}, {start: {_id:111}, end: {_id:112}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Psychogenic ED (based on global efficacy question) | RR 2.05 (95% CI 1.33 to 3.16) | Level I", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:10:32.367Z'), source_document:"SECTION 5: TRADITIONAL AND COMPLEMENTARY MEDICINE", source:"section-5-tcm.md"}}, {start: {_id:113}, end: {_id:45}, properties:{chunk_index:0, evidence:"Yohimbine | Reasonable therapeutic option compared with placebo; infrequent and reversible AEs | Level I", created_at:datetime('2026-04-30T12:10:32.45Z'), source_document:"SECTION 5: TRADIT